<!--
  modules/graphic_export/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 2 module POM (Wave B)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/graphic_export -am
  package from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/graphic_export/pom.xml
  package). Ant (modules/graphic_export/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains
  the real build; nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave B, and the reason renderer had to land in
  the SAME wave rather than a later one: graphic_export imports
  org.scilab.modules.renderer.JoGLView directly, so both are added to the
  parent's <modules> together, with renderer ordered first (confirmed by
  the Reactor Build Order preamble of a full `mvn clean package` — see the
  Stage 2-f Task 2 report).

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh graphic_export, 8 files):
    [1] imports (excluding own packages), verified per-file (all 8 files
        read directly, not just grepped) — every import below is REAL, none
        is a stray/unused line:
      - org.apache.batik.dom.GenericDOMImplementation, org.apache.batik.
        svggen.{SVGGeneratorContext, SVGGraphics2D} — Export.java. thirdparty/
        batik-all-1.17.jar, below (same jar, same coordinate as
        modules/helptools/pom.xml's identical dependency).
      - org.apache.fop.Version, org.apache.fop.svg.PDFDocumentGraphics2D —
        Export.java. thirdparty/fop-core-2.9.jar, below (same jar, same
        coordinate as modules/helptools/pom.xml's identical dependency;
        `unzip -l` confirms fop-core-2.9.jar — not the sibling fop-2.9.jar
        also under thirdparty/ — carries both classes plus
        org.apache.fop.apps.MimeConstants).
      - org.apache.xmlgraphics.java2d.GraphicContext, .java2d.ps.
        {AbstractPSDocumentGraphics2D, EPSDocumentGraphics2D,
        PSDocumentGraphics2D}, .ps.{DSCConstants, PSGenerator} —
        Export.java, all six DIRECTLY imported (contrast modules/
        helptools/pom.xml's xmlgraphics-commons finding, which needed the
        jar for an INHERITED constant with zero direct references anywhere
        in its source — this module's own code spells every one of these
        names out itself). Same jar, same coordinate as helptools'
        identical dependency: thirdparty/xmlgraphics-commons-2.9.jar.
      - org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.Canvas, .implementation.g2d.{G2DCanvas,
        G2DCanvasFactory}, .implementation.jogl.{JoGLCanvas,
        JoGLCanvasFactory} — Export.java. A REACTOR SIBLING (scirenderer,
        Stage 2-d), not a vendored jar — same as modules/renderer/pom.xml.
      - org.scilab.modules.commons.ScilabCommonsUtils; org.scilab.modules.
        graphic_objects.{axes.AxesContainer, figure.Figure,
        graphicController.GraphicController,
        graphicObject.GraphicObjectProperties, uicontrol.frame.Frame};
        org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages; org.scilab.modules.
        renderer.JoGLView.DrawerVisitor — four reactor dependencies below,
        commons/graphic_objects/localization already migrated, renderer
        migrated in THIS SAME WAVE (modules/renderer/pom.xml).
      - java.*, javax.imageio{,.stream}, org.w3c.dom.{DOMImplementation,
        Document} — JDK, not a dependency.
    [2] reflection targets — RULED OUT: org.freehep.graphicsio.emf.
        EMFGraphics2D, reached only via Export.java:1120's
        `Class.forName("org.freehep.graphicsio.emf.EMFGraphics2D")` inside
        EMFExporter's constructor (confirmed by reading the file: the
        loaded class is used purely reflectively, cast to the JDK's own
        Graphics2D, with a caught ClassNotFoundException that throws "This
        Scilab build does not provide EMF support" — EMF export is designed
        as an OPTIONAL, pluggable feature, not a hard compile-time
        dependency). Reproduced as an absence, not fixed into a real
        dependency — same discipline as modules/console/pom.xml's gui
        exclusion and modules/helptools/pom.xml's xcos exclusion.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import — ONE entry here needed
        opening the file, and it was a genuine false positive, not a
        dependency:
      - org.freehep.graphicsio.ImageEncoder — the ONLY hit is
        convertToPPM/PPMEncoder.java:43, `//import org.freehep.graphicsio.
        ImageEncoder;` — commented-out, dead code. PPMEncoder.java:54's
        `public class PPMEncoder extends ImageEncoder` resolves instead to
        the LOCAL class convertToPPM/ImageEncoder.java:59 (`public abstract
        class ImageEncoder implements ImageConsumer`, same package, no
        import needed) — confirmed by `find` + `grep -rn "class
        ImageEncoder"` across the module: exactly one definition, and it is
        graphic_export's own. This is precisely the over-report class
        [3]'s own header warns about (matches inside a comment) — the
        freehep jar this name superficially suggests is not needed for any
        reason.
      - Every other name (org.apache.batik.*, org.apache.fop.*, org.apache.
        xmlgraphics.*, org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.*, org.scilab.modules.*)
        already accounted for in [1].
  NET RESULT: no freehep-* jar of any kind appears in <dependencies> below,
  despite build.incl.xml:100-102 putting freehep-graphics2d.jar,
  freehep-graphicsio-emf.jar and freehep-graphicsio.jar on the SHARED
  compile classpath every module can see — graphic_export's own source
  genuinely uses none of them at compile time. Ant's shared classpath being
  available is not evidence a given module needs everything on it; only
  this module's own confirmed imports/FQNs are.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>graphic_export</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:20 <property name="library.title" value="Export plot to any image format"/> -->
  <name>Export plot to any image format</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.ScilabCommonsUtils — Export.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.{axes.AxesContainer,
         figure.Figure, graphicController.GraphicController,
         graphicObject.GraphicObjectProperties, uicontrol.frame.Frame} —
         Export.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>graphic_objects</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — Driver.java,
         FileExporter.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.renderer.JoGLView.DrawerVisitor — Export.java.
         THE WAVE'S NAMESAKE EDGE: renderer migrates in this same wave
         (modules/renderer/pom.xml), which is why both land together —
         see this file's header comment. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>renderer</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.Canvas, .implementation.g2d.*,
         .implementation.jogl.* — Export.java. A reactor sibling
         (scirenderer, Stage 2-d), not a vendored jar. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>scirenderer</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.apache.batik.dom.GenericDOMImplementation, org.apache.batik.
         svggen.{SVGGeneratorContext, SVGGraphics2D} — Export.java. Same
         jar, same coordinate as modules/helptools/pom.xml's identical
         dependency (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>batik-all</artifactId>
      <version>1.17</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.apache.fop.Version, org.apache.fop.svg.PDFDocumentGraphics2D —
         Export.java. Same jar, same coordinate as modules/helptools/
         pom.xml's identical dependency. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>fop-core</artifactId>
      <version>2.9</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.apache.xmlgraphics.java2d.GraphicContext, .java2d.ps.
         {AbstractPSDocumentGraphics2D, EPSDocumentGraphics2D,
         PSDocumentGraphics2D}, .ps.{DSCConstants, PSGenerator} —
         Export.java, all DIRECT imports (unlike modules/helptools/pom.xml's
         inherited-constant case for this same jar). Same jar, same
         coordinate as that module's identical dependency. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>xmlgraphics-commons</artifactId>
      <version>2.9</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/graphic_export/jar/org.scilab.modules.
                 graphic_export.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped:
                 Specification-Vendor and Implementation-Vendor both carried (now un-mangled to "è" by register P1)
                 the double-mangled "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see
                 modules/localization/pom.xml's fuller comment for the
                 mechanism. Implementation-Version is present, frozen at the
                 literal "00000000 0000", positioned between
                 Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
                 where Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
